Menu="UserPreferences"
Title="Custom Header Logo"
Icon="image"
---
<?php
/* Custom Header Logo - replace the Unraid logo and its link in the top banner.
 * Settings are stored on the flash drive and survive reboots and OS updates.
 */
$chl_cfg_file = '/boot/config/plugins/custom.header.logo/custom.header.logo.cfg';
$chl_cfg = is_file($chl_cfg_file) ? (parse_ini_file($chl_cfg_file) ?: []) : [];
$chl_service = $chl_cfg['SERVICE']     ?? 'disabled';
$chl_logourl = $chl_cfg['LOGOURL']     ?? '';
$chl_linkurl = $chl_cfg['LINKURL']     ?? '';
$chl_height  = $chl_cfg['HEIGHT']      ?? '28';
$chl_newtab  = $chl_cfg['NEWTAB']      ?? '0';
$chl_flash   = '';
$chl_flashv  = 0;
foreach (['svg','png','webp','jpg','jpeg','gif'] as $chl_ext) {
  $chl_path = "/boot/config/plugins/custom.header.logo/logo.$chl_ext";
  if (is_file($chl_path)) { $chl_flash = "logo.$chl_ext"; $chl_flashv = filemtime($chl_path); break; }
}
?>

<form markdown="1" name="custom_header_logo" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="custom.header.logo/custom.header.logo.cfg"/>

_(Enable custom logo)_:
: <select name="SERVICE">
  <?=mk_option($chl_service, "disabled", _('No'))?>
  <?=mk_option($chl_service, "enabled", _('Yes'))?>
  </select>

> Set to **Yes** to replace the stock Unraid logo in the top banner. Set to **No** to restore the original logo (refresh the page after applying).

_(Logo file)_:
: <span class="inline-block">
  <img id="chl-preview" src="<?=$chl_flash ? "/plugins/custom.header.logo/logo.php?v=$chl_flashv" : ''?>" alt="" style="height:28px;width:auto;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:10px;padding:4px;border:1px solid var(--border-color, #888);border-radius:4px;<?=$chl_flash ? '' : 'display:none;'?>">
  <span id="chl-none" style="margin-right:10px;<?=$chl_flash ? 'display:none;' : ''?>"><em>_(No logo uploaded)_</em></span>
  <input type="file" id="chl-file" accept=".png,.svg,.webp,.jpg,.jpeg,.gif,image/png,image/svg+xml,image/webp,image/jpeg,image/gif" style="display:none">
  <input type="button" id="chl-upload" value="_(Upload)_">
  <input type="button" id="chl-delete" value="_(Delete)_" <?=$chl_flash ? '' : 'disabled'?>>
  <span id="chl-msg" style="margin-left:10px"></span>
</span>

> Upload an image from this computer: it is stored on the flash drive and survives reboots and plugin updates. Takes effect immediately, no **Apply** needed.
> PNG, SVG, WebP, JPG or GIF, **max 512 KB**, ideally with a **transparent background**. **Suggested size: 320 x 56 px** (displayed at 160 x 28 px, matching the stock logo).
> You can also copy `logo.png` (or `.svg`, ...) into `config/plugins/custom.header.logo/` on the `flash` share.

_(Logo image URL)_:
: <input type="text" name="LOGOURL" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($chl_logourl, ENT_QUOTES)?>" maxlength="1024" placeholder="_(Optional: empty = uploaded logo)_">

> Optional: an http(s) URL to use **instead of** the uploaded logo. If the webGUI uses HTTPS, the image URL must be HTTPS too, or the browser blocks it.

_(Logo links to)_:
: <input type="text" name="LINKURL" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($chl_linkurl, ENT_QUOTES)?>" maxlength="1024" placeholder="https://example.com (empty = /Dashboard)">

> The page opened when the logo is clicked. Leave empty to link to the server Dashboard.

_(Logo height in pixels)_:
: <input type="number" name="HEIGHT" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($chl_height, ENT_QUOTES)?>" min="12" max="80" style="width:80px">

> Displayed height of the logo. Default **28** (stock logo height). Width scales automatically. The banner is 90 px tall, so values above 80 are clamped.

_(Open link in a new tab)_:
: <select name="NEWTAB">
  <?=mk_option($chl_newtab, "0", _('No'))?>
  <?=mk_option($chl_newtab, "1", _('Yes'))?>
  </select>

> Only the logo is replaced: the Unraid version and update indicator next to it are kept.

&nbsp;
: <span class="inline-block">
  <input type="submit" name="#apply" value="_(Apply)_" disabled>
  <input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
</span>

</form>

<p><em>Changes take effect after a page refresh. Settings are stored on the flash drive and re-applied automatically at every boot.</em></p>

<script>
(function() {
  var file = document.getElementById('chl-file');
  var preview = document.getElementById('chl-preview');
  var none = document.getElementById('chl-none');
  var del = document.getElementById('chl-delete');
  var msg = document.getElementById('chl-msg');

  function say(text, ok) {
    msg.textContent = text;
    msg.className = ok ? 'green-text' : 'red-text';
  }

  function show(v) {
    var src = v ? '/plugins/custom.header.logo/logo.php?v=' + v : '';
    preview.src = src;
    preview.style.display = v ? '' : 'none';
    none.style.display = v ? 'none' : '';
    del.disabled = !v;
    // Live-update the banner when it already uses the uploaded logo.
    var banner = document.querySelector('#chl-logo img');
    if (banner && src && banner.src.indexOf('/plugins/custom.header.logo/logo.php') !== -1) { banner.src = src; return true; }
    return false;
  }

  // Same transport as the webGUI's own FileUpload.php: the file travels as a base64
  // data URL in a plain urlencoded jQuery POST, to which the webGUI's global
  // $.ajaxPrefilter appends csrf_token. No multipart/FormData: it does not get
  // through on real servers. A timeout guarantees every outcome ends with a message.
  function post(data, done) {
    try {
      $.ajax({
        url: '/plugins/custom.header.logo/upload.php', type: 'POST',
        data: data, dataType: 'json', timeout: 30000
      }).done(function(res) {
        done(res || { error: 'Empty response' });
      }).fail(function(xhr, status, err) {
        var res = xhr.responseJSON;
        if (!res) { try { res = JSON.parse(xhr.responseText); } catch (e) {} }
        done({ error: (res && res.error) || (status === 'timeout' ? 'No response from the server (timeout)' : 'HTTP ' + xhr.status + ' ' + (err || status)) });
      });
    } catch (e) {
      done({ error: 'Error: ' + e.message });
    }
  }

  document.getElementById('chl-upload').addEventListener('click', function() { file.click(); });

  file.addEventListener('change', function(e) {
    e.stopPropagation();
    var f = file.files[0];
    file.value = '';
    if (!f) return;
    if (f.size > 512 * 1024) { say('File too large (max 512 KB)', false); return; }
    var reader = new FileReader();
    reader.onerror = function() { say('Could not read the file', false); };
    reader.onload = function() {
      say('Uploading...', true);
      post({ cmd: 'upload', filedata: reader.result }, function(res) {
        if (res.ok) say('Saved as ' + res.file + '.' + (show(res.v) ? '' : ' Refresh the page to see it in the banner.'), true);
        else say(res.error || 'Upload failed', false);
      });
    };
    reader.readAsDataURL(f);
  });

  del.addEventListener('click', function() {
    post({ cmd: 'delete' }, function(res) {
      if (res.ok) { show(0); say('Logo deleted. Refresh the page to update the banner.', true); }
      else say(res.error || 'Delete failed', false);
    });
  });
})();
</script>
